  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 104 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nMedium range forecast guidance is struggling with how to handle a \nbroad forward-tilt trough axis entering the Great Basin and Rockies \nFriday and Saturday. Cluster analysis yesterday was favoring a more \nprogressive and drier trough passage but has now trended toward a\nweak closed H5 low over far southwest NM, including the GFS and \nECMWF AI solutions. Slightly better moisture as well has increased\nchances for some rain showers over the southwest higher terrain \nFriday afternoon. This activity may spread northeast toward the \nABQ metro area Friday evening before the focus shifts to southeast\nNM Saturday. NBM 50th percentile QPF amounts are <0.20\" near the \nsouthern high terrain. The latest RRFS is however more aggressive \nwith a couple QPF streaks >0.40\" with bands of showers. \n\nGuidance still shows a weak ridge forming over the southern Rockies \nSunday thru Tuesday with light winds, warming temps, and decreasing \nhumidity.",
